      "label": "The woman is mapped as 'someone who doesn't like the sun'",
      "description": "The text 'i don't like the sun' is mapped onto the visual entity 'woman', implying that she is the person who doesn't like the sun. This is a direct analogical mapping where the textual entity 'i' (the speaker) is projected onto the visual entity 'woman'. The woman's presence on the beach while wearing a visor, combined with the text, creates a humorous or ironic contrast that reinforces this mapping.",
